# game-derived bytes (extract-field 2800) -- provenance gate: NEVER commit
*.bgx
*.bgi

# game-derived GEOMETRY -- quay_marker.obj is a verbatim copy of stock FF9's Block[21][10] Object
# mesh (312 verts + UVs + normals lifted from p0data). Same class as the battle-map FBX / minted-scene
# raw16 in ff9mapkit/docs/PROVENANCE.md: read from YOUR install, gitignored, never committed.
# `mint_quay_marker.py` regenerates it from your own install -- the SCRIPT is the committed part.
*.obj

# ...but the quay_beacon meshes are OUR OWN procedural geometry (mint_quay_beacon.py -- no game bytes
# at all, only UV coordinates pointing into the shared atlas), so the provenance rule above does not
# apply and they are committed alongside their generator. One per Southern Ring quay.
!quay_beacon.obj
!quay_beacon_*.obj
